{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778346497,"nonce":"m4JtBMveu05dZJw6//+0Gb1+Mgc=","title":"plot.loss_history extension: multi-run comparison with shared term axes","message":"The existing `feedbax.plot.loss_history` utility (feedbax/plot/plotly.py ~line 39) handles term overlay within a single run with replicate error bands. A common analysis use case is comparing N runs of the same training script (or close variants) on a shared set of loss-term axes with replicate error bands per run.\n\nHand-rolling plotly for this each time loses styling consistency and requires duplicating the per-term aggregation logic. Surfaced from rlrmp work in `_artifacts/part2_5/runpod/anti_anticipation_loss_shape_6cell/figures/training_loss/figure.html` (6-cell anti-anticipation + loss-shape matrix).\n\nLightweight extension proposal: a `loss_history_compare(histories: dict[str, TaskTrainerHistory], **kwargs)` function that takes a labelled dict of histories and overlays one trace per label with the same per-term aggregation (mean + error band across replicates) as the single-run version. Ideally shares all axis/layout/colour logic with the existing utility.\n\nSurfaced from rlrmp; tracking issue 2bc95fd.","files":null}]}